tor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DdUJ2euN3sieyVz5RLisFC", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376876, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DdUJ2euN3sieyVz5RLisFC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381074, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It now rounds 2.675 to 2.68 and 2.665 to 2.66, which is what `tests/test_money.py` expects. This was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it directly. I went by the test and the docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Cyp9LzYkLBY3VNNYp8UXi1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012iPiB2Zip5D8LtpucEozCw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PbCewLMxzSvkxQ1Q5h54VN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FwD1Msh8JsvqCZHuvEcfhG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013cLNTziy4AEprYhH2E243M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P5Wz8sQu9HW6JaoEfoBt3X", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VpTSBVYMT46tddLMikVMLd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DdUJ2euN3sieyVz5RLisFC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\nThis PR switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It now rounds 2.675 to 2.68 and 2.665 to 2.66, which is what `tests/test_money.py` expects. This was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it directly. I went by the test and the docstring.", "type": "text"}]}]}